<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thane</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sthanaka</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thane is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the Thane creek just north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Mumbai</a>. Known in medieval inscriptions as Sthanaka, it was a centre of the Silahara kings of the North Konkan and a port visited by Arab traders and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marco-polo">Marco Polo</a>. Later held by the Portuguese and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a>, it was the terminus of India's first passenger railway from Bombay in 1853.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thane.jpg" alt="Thane" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mehulsg · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hiranandaniestate.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
